# Stage 0 baseline: inventory and feasibility

**Status:** in progress  
**Initial baseline:** 2026-10-18 21:50 +07  
**Physical inventory update:** 2026-10-24  
**Classification:** AUDIT / DOCUMENTATION  
**Owner:** HAVEN for platform feasibility; ELMOS for host reproducibility; KDAL for interface fit  
**Thesis relevance:** establishes what can be tested and what claims are currently unsupported before selecting a research question.

This is a working evidence record under the workspace scope contract. It is
not a new repository, approved research question, implementation plan, or board
support declaration. `unknown` means no qualifying observation has been
collected yet.

## Physical inventory update (2026-10-24)

The workspace owner reports that no Radxa Orion O6/O6N or Orange Pi 6/6 Plus
physical SBCs are currently available, and that no boot logs exist. The owner
also reports that the essential board documents and components were downloaded
from official webpages. Third-party and community checkouts remain identified
by their own upstream provenance. Original download URLs are not yet recorded
alongside every local file, so preserve this as reported provenance until URLs
are added to the source ledger.

This blocks board boot, EL2-entry, interrupt, DMA/SMMU, and performance
experiments for all four boards. It does not block continued source audits,
host workflow work, QEMU checks, literature review, or research-question
framing. Do not describe the physical targets as verified or probe-ready while
hardware is unavailable.

